WHAT THE BATTERIES ARE, AND WHAT THEY ARE NOT
  The batteries under batteries/ are our own constructions. Their LABELS derive from third-party
  facts — en.wikipedia pageview counts, ClinicalTrials.gov posting dates — which are the property
  of their respective sources and are used here as timestamps and counts, not as content. The
  entity strings are public names. Nothing in this licence grants rights over the upstream
  sources.

  The corpora scored in the audit table (geometry-of-truth, truth-is-universal,
  hallucinated-references, bielik-entity-familiarity) are NOT distributed here and are NOT covered
  by this licence. They are fetched from their own repositories under their own terms; the audit
  records a URL and a sha256, not a copy.

ON THE VERDICTS
  A DISQUALIFIED verdict from this tool is a measurement about a corpus, not a finding of error or
  misconduct by its authors. The tool is offered so that anyone can run it against anything —
  including everything we have published. Four of our own nine batteries fail it, and those rows
  are at the top of our own audit table.

  The tool's own false-positive rate is measured, not asserted: at 500 seeds per grid row, every
  construction sits below the 10% ceiling with the upper bound of an exact 95% interval. Run
  `python3 nulltest.py --calibrate` and check it yourself. That measurement is ours and has no
  external co-signer, which is a limitation we state rather than one you should discover.
